{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn","id":902383,"title":"Heretical Thoughts on Unicorn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-28T17:27:55-07:00","id":902383,"title":"Heretical Thoughts on Unicorn","content":"As some people who follow my posts know, I have issues with Werewolf. I think too often the game becomes an unintentional parody of Captain Planet forcing left wing politics down people's throat instead of being a game of &quot;savage horror&quot; inspired by actual werewolf lore in mythology, folk tales, literature, and cinema. So in my games, I make alterations that keep the game's bones while developing it a little bit differently. Every now and again, I post these differences for the benefit of the forum. If they can make something out of it for their games, all the better. And I don't mind if people disagree with me or think I'm wrong. De gustibus non est disputandum.<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia tribe is somewhat problematic. Although the tribe has its fans, it seems like many players have issues with the depiction of the Children of Gaia. Their tribebooks are among the most reviled in fandom (anytime it comes up on this or other forums, many people explain their dislike of them). The major reason is that the tribe seems to be at odds with the concept of the Garou in general, and this tension has not been handled well.<br /> <br /> I think the big reason why is how the totem of unicorn is handled, and how unicorn is depicted in the game setting. Simply put, it is not the unicorn of legend, but the unicorn of Saturday morning cartoons and children's toys \u2013 Unicorn as My Little Pony. I think if the legends of unicorn are actually consulted, a different interpretation of the totem and therefore the tribe can be used that would better integrate the Children with the Garou.<br /> <br /> This is not the My Little Pony interpretation of unicorn, but I will attempt to preserve the essentials of the Tribe. I think any valid interpretation must cover the important events and aspects of the Tribe. I consider these to be those elements:<ul><li>They opposed the Impergium.</li> <li>They are the primary foes of the Defiler Wyrm among the Garou.</li> <li>They stress the need for unity and cooperation among the Garou Nation.</li> <li>They have a tendency to seek the leadership of the Garou Nation or otherwise consider themselves the \u201ctrue\u201d Garou.</li> </ul>The next few posts lay out some of my thinking. I am breaking them into separate posts because I think it aids readability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-28-2016, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:29:07-07:00","id":902384,"title":"","content":"Here are some points about unicorns in real legend and folklore.<ul><li>Unicorns represent the power and sanctity of the unspoiled wilderness. They are paragons of purity.</li> <li>Unicorns are untamed animals, always deadly and ferocious.</li> <li>The pride and ferocity of the unicorn meant it would not allow itself to be taken alive.</li> <li>Unicorns are considered to be among the most, if not the most, magnificent and beautiful beasts.</li> <li>Unicorns are a protectors of purity and defender of the innocent such as virgin maidens and children. Unicorns pay homage to their purity and gentleness.</li> <li>Karkadanns were the unicorns of Persia and India. They were very dangerous.</li> <li>Legend said that the horse of Alexander the Great, Boucephalous, was a unicorn.</li> <li>The horn of a unicorn has healing properties.</li> <li>Natural history places the unicorn in India (probably because they were tales of the Indian rhinoceros).</li> <li>In older times, the unicorn and lion fought over who would rule the wilderness. There was a seasonal exchange \u2013 unicorns' power was greater in spring, but the lion increased in the summer.</li> </ul>Two important call outs \u2013 nowhere are unicorns associated with either \u201cpeace\u201d or \u201clove\u201d. These are not intrinsic properties of unicorns. At best they are emergent properties based on their purity and tales of innocence taming them.<br /> <br /> The essentials of Unicorn as a totem are thus:<ul><li>A paragon and protector of purity.</li> <li>A creature that is untamed and ferocious.</li> <li>A healer as well as a warrior.</li> <li>A magnificent beast who is a natural leader of the wilderness.</li> </ul>\u201cPeace\u201d by itself is not one of its properties, although we can see the reasons why promoting peace became a goal. Originally it was in service of its original totemic goals, but later became a goal in itself \u2013 probably as a result of a particularly successful Camp in pushing its political goals.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the association unicorn has with virginity places it directly opposed to many concepts the Tribebook has associated with \u201clove\u201d, particularly physical sex acts.<br /> <br /> The \u201cburned out hippies\u201d image which plagues the Tribe does represent some of its members. Whether this represents a minority of majority of the Tribe is dependent on the ST, but for my own chronicles I make this group those who inadvertently serve the Wyrm \u2013 they represent a corruption of Unicorn's children who hide behind a false interpretation of the totem and the tribe while failing to achieve the true qualities of the Totem. It is unlikely such people were able to pass their tribal Rite of Passage if they were like this as cubs, so it must be a phenomenon that happens afterwards. (Not all \u201chippies\u201d are \u201cburned out\u201d, so even in my chronicle I have stalwart \u201cgranola eaters\u201d as upstanding members of the tribe.)<br /> <br /> The role of unicorn as a ruler of the wilderness in rival to lion shows a great insight on why the Children of Gaia have tried to lead the Garou Nation in various forms. The nature of the totem keeps pushing its children \u2013 the tribe \u2013 into that role.<br /> <br /> Why do the Children of Gaia rage? They rage in defense of purity, particularly when it is threatened by the Defiler Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia opposed the Impergium not out of a sense of non-violence. They opposed it because 1) they thought the innocent were being killed, and 2) they feared the Garou's heart were being corrupted \u2013 instead of bravely fighting the Wyrm in its lair, they were killing helpless people \u2013 the Wyrm was both corrupting the courage of the Garou and making them cruel and despicable. This was later twisted \u2013 likely quite lately, perhaps as a result of prolonged exposure to Christianity in Europe during the Dark Ages \u2013 as a general desire for non-violence, peace, or compassion. Means became ends over the course of centuries. This process would be accelerated later as Humanism, the Enlightenment, and international pacifism took hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-28-2016, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:31:05-07:00","id":902386,"title":"","content":"Let's look how this impacts the current setting if you want to include some of these ideas in your chronicles.<br /> <br /> First, it provides a basis for Children of Gaia to be more fierce and warlike \u2013 something many players seem to want to justify.<br /> <br /> Second, the burned out hippies interpretation isn't seen as the basis fo the tribe, but is a weakness or corruption of it. How extensive that corruption is, is up to you. Of course, the burned out hippies deny that entirely and see themselves as the embodiment of unicorn's desire. Most of them haven't fallen to the extent that they detect as Wyrm tainted. But the worst of them do end up corrupted, but so do members of other tribes, so that doesn't prove anything, does it? They would make interesting foils or even villains (for those who have gone off the deep end).<br /> <br /> Third, there is still a roll for granola eaters in the tribe as defenders of purity and the unspoiled wilderness. These would be the stereotypical good aspects of hippies without those elements seen as negative.<br /> <br /> Fourth, the desire of the Children to lead the Garou Nation gives them a harder edge than is typical for the tribe in canon. They are not ambitious like the Shadow Lords, but they could be seen as one of the tribes most likely to challenge the Silver Fangs for leadership of the Nation. This actually fits with some of the ambitious statements found in the tribebooks which give the Children a leadership or dominant role.<br /> <br /> Fifth, there is a role for fierce, combatant Children of Gaia \u2013 the untamed karkadann of the tribe. This is not some anomalous role that requires tortured explanation. It is at the heart of the tribe as the defenders of the unspoiled wilderness, and represented by the \u201cblack unicorn\u201d spirit. This camp is probably on fairly good terms with the Red Talons, normally a tribe in opposition to the Children. They don't want to kill humans, but they defend the remaining areas of pristine wilderness. There is probably a very strong lupus presence in this group.<br /> <br /> So that's it. Not very much different from the tribe as is, but with a few different emphases that I think puts the tribe into a better situation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:55:38-07:00","id":902399,"title":"","content":"This is pretty neat. It keeps the tribal origins and goals similar, but gives them a better edge.<br /> <br /> But what about the converts? A huge part of the tribe is that they take in metis from other tribes and even redeemed Dancers. How does that figure to your take on the Children of Gaia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:56:11-07:00","id":902400,"title":"","content":"Never felt like left wing politics were forced down my throat.<br /> <br /> then again, forcing environmentalism down my throat, is kind of like trying to force racism down Hitlers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:05:53-07:00","id":902403,"title":"","content":"I hadn't given any thought to that to be honest, but this is an important role of the tribe. It probably has to do with all metis are obviously babies when they are born. And babies are innocent, even if their parents sinned. As protectors of purity and innocence, the Children would presumably take them (and any other children) abandoned by the other tribes.<br /> <br /> In terms of converts - talking about adults here, particularly those who already were accepted by other tribes, but then left - there is not a strong connection. It's probably a result of &quot;means becoming ends&quot; once again (Hey, we take in all these babies including metis, why wouldn't we accept adult converts?) plus the ongoing issue of Unicorn as a ruler of the wilderness. I think the early tribebook had some extreme language that the Children of Gaia had all of Gaia's realm as their territory and really pushed the Children as a tribe that should be dominant. If so, there may be a thinking that since Unicorn is the ruler, then everyone should be his Children and if so, why not take everyone.<br /> <br /> Of course, that does conflict to a degree with the idea that Unicorn is still selective with their Rites of Passage. Unicorn has to have some standards even if the tribe leaders have lowered theirs. It may be that the tests have been somewhat watered down over the years, or of a nature that isn't as challenging in certain areas as it should be. I would probably make the tests to win Unicorn as a pack totem for the Rite of the Totem much harder than it is to become a tribe member. A subtle clue that the tribe has perhaps become a bit more tolerant than it should be.<br /> <br /> I'll have to give that some more thought though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:19:30-07:00","id":902407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=902400#post902400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never felt like left wing politics were forced down my throat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind the environmental angle and think it has a relevant role to play in a society of primitive earth based religion shamans. However, there is some over the top stuff in some supplements, and it is obvious some writers thought they were preaching to the choir and only that. I actually like a lot of Rage Across New York, but was bewildered and confused that the major evil group in New York City was a left wing caricature of right wing Republicans in a city and area of the country which is not a base of right wing Republicans in the country. Even the few Republican mayors of New York have been part of the liberal/progressive wing of the Republican Party since the start of the 20th century. It was totally inappropriate for the bad guys here (it would be less inappropriate if the chronicle was based in a region known for right wing politics). If you were looking for problems in pre-Giulani New York City, their origins shouldn't be in some right wing caricature. Any Wyrm cult should be using the cover of some leftist group if the writer was going to go down a political route.<br /> <br /> I do think the environmental angle was been pushed too much though - the Garou badly need other antagonists for variety that should still be appropriate. I am actually preparing my &quot;Rage Across the Miskatonic&quot; series on how to inject enemies appropriate for the cosmic horror genre into the game, but am not quite ready for that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:55:48-07:00","id":902457,"title":"","content":"oh thoughts on my question on Hunters Hunted style hunters, about some idiot that thinks hes the &quot;Ultimate game hunter&quot; <br /> <br /> seems likely to be a lampoonish self removing inconvenience","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:44:19-07:00","id":902676,"title":"","content":"I like this...I have never been a fan of the CoG because while their core write up seems interesting the tribe books and other source material (Rage Across Australia) has handled them so poorly over the years, I never liked them. I have a player who is a huge fan boy but he grips tightly to the core book write up in place of the tribe books. I'd been planning on something similar to this in my game where you have the tribe book version of the tribe, and what the tribe should be as a divide in the CoG. I'm going to steal some of the stuff you posted here. Maybe even make two different unicorns...having one be a bit of an imposter that many CoG mistakenly take their cues form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:03:11-07:00","id":902783,"title":"","content":"i would like to point out that environmentalism can be a deeply conservative almost v\u00f6lkisch thing as well. This would work well with your purity argument and would bring parts of the CoG closer to the Get of Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:18:51-07:00","id":902828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=902783#post902783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i would like to point out that environmentalism can be a deeply conservative almost v\u00f6lkisch thing as well. This would work well with your purity argument and would bring parts of the CoG closer to the Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Get don't quite do that anymore, except for that one camp. Which is living on borrowed time, since one of the metaplot events was &quot;the Fenrir get tired of the Swords of Heimdall being racist tools and kill them all&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:35:16-07:00","id":902843,"title":"","content":"Something i always considered to be a mistake. Let us just look at the rise of popular nationalism all over the real world. Maybe they would rename and rebrand themselves (with the help of the CoG <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) to be more moderate and more territorial. Along the lines of:<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah i don't care who and what you are, as long as you stay out of our territory.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T12:39:45-07:00","id":902943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=902843#post902843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something i always considered to be a mistake. Let us just look at the rise of popular nationalism all over the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Get venerate the enemy of the chief Germanic deity, who is destined to take out said deity while his sons snack on everyone identified as &quot;Odinson&quot;. If you're going all the way with your Germanic stylings into very recent by the standards of Garou society racist idiocy, that's a pretty big hurdle to cross. Honestly, given how much Glass Walkers chase transient human fads, they should be the ones most likely to have a stained history in this regard, or to have lost a camp to it through necessary purges of their number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:48:33-07:00","id":902988,"title":"","content":"Odin is the Nordic not the Germanic name, but i am splitting hairs here. I just feel that people give away too much flavor. I had a similar problem with the DA:V Lasombra, everything getting nice and tidy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T15:16:14-07:00","id":903042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=902988#post902988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odin is the Nordic not the Germanic name, but i am splitting hairs here.</div> </div> </div> </div>An undead necromancer is an undead necromancer, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just feel that people give away too much flavor. I had a similar problem with the DA:V Lasombra, everything getting nice and tidy. </div> </div> </div>The Swords weren't flavor. They were the result of poor research. Poor research should be corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T16:09:52-07:00","id":903072,"title":"","content":"If it is not important why are you using the word Germanic. <br /> <br /> I read your argument with heinrich about it. I don't think there is much to add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T16:45:38-07:00","id":903100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=902783#post902783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i would like to point out that environmentalism can be a deeply conservative almost v\u00f6lkisch thing as well. This would work well with your purity argument and would bring parts of the CoG closer to the Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to get into political debates other than to &quot;open up the game&quot; and allow other ideas to enter. I do agree that there is an environmental consciousness on the right as on the left. Many people do not seem to realize that Hitler and the Nazis actually implemented the first environmental laws in world history. Actually, the incipient environmental movements of Germany in the early twentieth century pretty much is the origins for the environmental movement of the 1960s and beyond. The Nazi version of it was just one facet or expression of it. (this is getting off topic, but I always felt it would be quite easy to explain why the Get of Fenris became involved in the Nazi movement since the Nazis actually have a lot of precepts that fit into Garou concepts).<br /> <br /> I don't think concepts of racial purity have much to do with pristine wilderness and uncorrupted innocence that Unicorn would espouse. While there might be some room for a kind of &quot;blood and soil&quot; nationalism int he Children, I think their stress on being an ecumenical movement among the Garou would really limit that memes growth among the children. Unlike some tribes, there is not a strong tie between the Tribe's kinfolk and a single ethnic or superethnic group. The backgrounds of tribe members are just too varied for this idea. It would be too divisive. Some kind of &quot;back to nature&quot; movement fits in with the tribe, but I don't think it'd be anything as extreme as the Nazi style. Some kind of general eugenics movement I could see the Children supporting, and this was in fact a big progressive cause until the Nazi version of it discredited it. Of course, it is beginning to make something of a comeback, but we're probably still a decade or two away before it becomes respectable.<br /> <br /> However, Tolkien would be a good example of a typical conservative's view of environmental stewardship. The old fashioned kind of English Tory landowner who enjoys the countryside and village life and not fond of the urban business world. That has nothing to do with racial purity, and could be the basis of a &quot;conservative&quot; wing of the Children of Gaia. However, I've always considered the Children to be too ideologically or idea oriented for them to be well represented by that. That's how I'd more see some of the Silver Fangs and the other tribes.<br /> <br /> If there are &quot;conservative&quot; Children, I'd imagine they'd be the remnants of some previous philosophy that found acceptance among the Children, but which has since lost relevance as they moved onto the next big thing. There might be some Children kinfolk still really into Catholic social teaching and the tradition of stewardship going back to St Francis of Assisi. I could see that being part of the tribe's history in Europe, but nowadays such adherents likely stick out like a sore thumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T17:17:10-07:00","id":903123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903072#post903072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is not important why are you using the word Germanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was being overly flowery? The Aesir, in any given language, were the enemies of the Get of Fenris. They're anti-pagans, in this respect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I read your argument with heinrich about it. I don't think there is much to add. </div> </div> </div>Not even the Glass Walkers being way more into hanging around human politicians and dwellings, and more likely to have contact with or even support nationalistic ideologies? Because the other tribes tend to live out in the sticks and rip apart any humans who steps foot into their territory as a matter of grave spiritual importance. They have the real scoop on their own people and of how the cosmos works, so why would they so many of them get won over to an ideology sold to them by people making factories and threatening their position?<br /> <br /> Because the flavor of the Get of Fenris isn't getting taken in by human racists. It's that they're even more extreme about being mighty warriors, and put more stock in it, than any other tribe, and so typically end up getting entangled in even worse trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T04:16:57-07:00","id":903385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903100#post903100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, Tolkien would be a good example of a typical conservative's view of environmental stewardship. The old fashioned kind of English Tory landowner who enjoys the countryside and village life and not fond of the urban business world. That has nothing to do with racial purity, and could be the basis of a &quot;conservative&quot; wing of the Children of Gaia. However, I've always considered the Children to be too ideologically or idea oriented for them to be well represented by that. That's how I'd more see some of the Silver Fangs and the other tribes.<br /> <br /> If there are &quot;conservative&quot; Children, I'd imagine they'd be the remnants of some previous philosophy that found acceptance among the Children, but which has since lost relevance as they moved onto the next big thing. There might be some Children kinfolk still really into Catholic social teaching and the tradition of stewardship going back to St Francis of Assisi. I could see that being part of the tribe's history in Europe, but nowadays such adherents likely stick out like a sore thumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something we all agree upon! talking about catholic social teaching it is likely that at least some of them could see that as something worthwhile. I would not think thy would go Nazi themselves however they could be enabler. The question would be if that is actually something that anyone would enjoy playing though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903123#post903123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was being overly flowery? The Aesir, in any given language, were the enemies of the Get of Fenris. They're anti-pagans, in this respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The humans had so much wrong i would not pay too much attention to paganism. Let us not forget that in nordic mythology Loki is Fenris father and a half giant, while being brother to the wyrm. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903123#post903123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even the Glass Walkers being way more into hanging around human politicians and dwellings, and more likely to have contact with or even support nationalistic ideologies? Because the other tribes tend to live out in the sticks and rip apart any humans who steps foot into their territory as a matter of grave spiritual importance. They have the real scoop on their own people and of how the cosmos works, so why would they so many of them get won over to an ideology sold to them by people making factories and threatening their position?<br /> <br /> Because the flavor of the Get of Fenris isn't getting taken in by human racists. It's that they're even more extreme about being mighty warriors, and put more stock in it, than any other tribe, and so typically end up getting entangled in even worse trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me the Get have certain similarities with Klingons. Just on steroids. They are proud of their heritage, proud of their Tribe and proud to be the tip of the spear. While racism might not be the best thing, their elitism has to be somewhat present and it would make sense to have a camp that does exactly that. This camp could have strong conservative tendencies and could add flavor. They would say the exact thing you would say &quot;(...)why would they so many of them get won over to an ideology sold to them by people making factories and threatening their position?&quot; is an inherent small-c conservative statement in my opinion. <br /> <br /> We also could say that all Fenris are like that and therefore no camp is needed, which is something i rather dislike as it gets misused by PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T07:15:58-07:00","id":903470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903385#post903385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The humans had so much wrong i would not pay too much attention to paganism. Let us not forget that in nordic mythology Loki is Fenris father and a half giant, while being brother to the wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's that tiny matter of &quot;fought these fucking mythological figures for generations&quot; complicating that. All of the camps named for Aesir are on the fringes of the Fenrir for exactly that reason; they're rightfully seen as dangerously unstable and not as focused on their actual tasks compared to the body of the tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me the Get have certain similarities with Klingons. Just on steroids. They are proud of their heritage, proud of their Tribe and proud to be the tip of the spear. While racism might not be the best thing, their elitism has to be somewhat present and it would make sense to have a camp that does exactly that. </div> </div> </div>Their heritage from Fenris. The enemy of all good Nords and Germans. And as for the, ideology, it would have been one that could potentially leave their kinfolk out in the cold, since they never thought that it was important to solely breed with pale people from Northern and Western Europe, and adoption of other Garou who could fight up to their standards with no other bias would naturally see a more diverse array of people in the tribe than some people seem to want to be the case.<br /> <br /> Seriously, they're not human and never were. They should have heaps of nothing but disdain for the dumbass racial theories of the colonial era.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This camp could have strong conservative tendencies and could add flavor. They would say the exact thing you would say &quot;(...)why would they so many of them get won over to an ideology sold to them by people making factories and threatening their position?&quot; is an inherent small-c conservative statement in my opinion.<br /> <br /> We also could say that all Fenris are like that and therefore no camp is needed, which is something i rather dislike as it gets misused by PCs. </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of those types would likely die the moment they went into apoplexy and lost their shit at a non-white Fenrir of higher Rank being treated with due respect, and probably end up dying before they could start would could actually be called a camp. The Get are, after all, too brutal for fragile human sensibilities, and racist ideologies tend to produce incredibly fragile egos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:05:06-07:00","id":903588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903470#post903470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's that tiny matter of &quot;fought these fucking mythological figures for generations&quot; complicating that. All of the camps named for Aesir are on the fringes of the Fenrir for exactly that reason; they're rightfully seen as dangerously unstable and not as focused on their actual tasks compared to the body of the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they still like the corax, who use Nordic mythology as well as very openly use Odins ravens for one of their camps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903470#post903470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Their heritage from Fenris. The enemy of all good Nords and Germans.</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading through the story again, it is clear that Loki prompted Odin to attack and while he is the arch nemesis of the Get of Fenris. Other important Gods are not mentioned. I did not see any mention of Freya, Frigg or Thor in that part which is rather sad.<br /> On the Other hand Tyr - who is portrayed as a Fenrir who would be an Aesir according to human myths. I would therefore not agree with that, as we have here a much more complex conflict on our hands. In the tribe book it says that Loki had to use sorcerers tricks to create an image of the Fenris trying to conquer their neighbors.<br /> In the next line it says that the Fenris wouldn't have to gain anything from conquering them, which is quite frankly not very persuading. The Get pretty much conquer everything that they can. &quot;Oh your lands lacks in protection, let us &quot;help&quot; you &quot;protecting&quot; it.&quot;<br /> <br /> To me this sounds as the Aesir where non Gaian spirits (not categorically Fomori or at least not at first) who had quite a bit of cloud themselves and the conflict was not as black and white as the Skalds are telling everyone.<br /> <br /> I know that is all interpretation, but it makes more sense - or at least in my head - than what we have in the books. It would retcon quite a bit, but it would also show the real problem that the Get have - they are a might makes right tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903470#post903470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as for the, ideology, it would have been one that could potentially leave their kinfolk out in the cold, since they never thought that it was important to solely breed with pale people from Northern and Western Europe, and adoption of other Garou who could fight up to their standards with no other bias would naturally see a more diverse array of people in the tribe than some people seem to want to be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>How likely is it that a non &quot;Pale&quot; werewolf would go to such a tribe in the first place though? After all the tribe in Europe would be predominantly Germanic/Nordic/Slavic as other ethnicities kinfolk is not that easy to come by there. And if there is any kind of pure breed in play, they would lose all of it as well. You . While there definitely are non Indo-Germanic ethnic Garou in the Tribe of the Get i do feel that the majority is still pretty much Indo-Germanic with some Slavic and some Celtic strings as most oft their kinfolk is very likely to be from those regions of the earth where the big majority of the population is Slavic, Germanic or Celtic.<br /> <br /> Your last sentence is not very straight forward. How much % would you think are non Germanic/Nordic/Slavic Get of Fenris? 7,5-10% in the in total? Maybe between 1/6 and 1/5 in the US? Sounds reasonably to me.<br /> <br /> I do have to say that this reminds me a bit of the controversy that the video game &quot;The Witcher&quot; had, when people felt that there weren't enough PoC.<br /> <br /> What they could conquer some PoC kinfolk and have children with it that should be very clear and while a ton of Kinfolk there are 100% some lines that derived from the sacking of Rome who are Italians and the ones that got conquered from the<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903470#post903470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, they're not human and never were. They should have heaps of nothing but disdain for the dumbass racial theories of the colonial era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elitism is not a new concept, they would go with the kinfolk that a.) is available and b.) is strong enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903470#post903470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vast majority of those types would likely die the moment they went into apoplexy and lost their shit at a non-white Fenrir of higher Rank being treated with due respect, and probably end up dying before they could start would could actually be called a camp. The Get are, after all, too brutal for fragile human sensibilities, and racist ideologies tend to produce incredibly fragile egos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, as many racists are often still functional members of their societies. They are definitely too brutal for any sensibilities, which would make any individual werewolf that is not of their kin not very likely to join them, wouldn't it? In fact i would think they are one of the tribes that lose the most cubs to other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8249,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","user":"Crytash","date":".  spelling 05-30-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:43:27-07:00","id":903611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903588#post903588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they still like the corax, who use Nordic mythology as well as very openly use Odins ravens for one of their camps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corax didn't get as much revised fluff. They'd probably go into detail about a slightly different setup otherwise, since otherwise the Fenrir would have had a very different reaction to them (see also the things that look like ravens in the story of Uli Brightjaws)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After reading through the story again, it is clear that Loki prompted Odin to attack and while he is the arch nemesis of the Get of Fenris. Other important Gods are not mentioned. I did not see any mention of Freya, Frigg or Thor in that part which is rather sad. </div> </div> </div>It had other things to get to, presumably. It can't just talk about this with all of its wordcount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the Other hand Tyr - who is portrayed as a Fenrir who would be an Aesir according to human myths. I would therefore not agree with that, as we have here a much more complex conflict on our hands. In the tribe book it says that Loki had to use sorcerers tricks to create an image of the Fenris trying to conquer their neighbors. </div> </div> </div>Tyr got his hand bitten off. Tyr isn't of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the next line it says that the Fenris wouldn't have to gain anything from conquering them, which is quite frankly not very persuading. The Get pretty much conquer everything that they can. &quot;Oh your lands lacks in protection, let us &quot;help&quot; you &quot;protecting&quot; it.&quot; </div> </div> </div>The tribe presumably changed after the experience of fighting the Aesir. Also, they might not have had high numbers at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me this sounds as the Aesir where non Gaian spirits (not categorically Fomori or at least not at first) who had quite a bit of cloud themselves and the conflict was not as black and white as the Skalds are telling everyone. </div> </div> </div>It's <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Odin,_The_All-High\" target=\"_blank\">a bit worse than that</a> for the Aesir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that is all interpretation, but it makes more sense - or at least in my head - than what we have in the books. It would retcon quite a bit, but it would also show the real problem that the Get have - they are a might makes right tribe. </div> </div> </div>Among might makes right tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How likely is it that a non &quot;Pale&quot; werewolf would go to such a tribe in the first place though? After all the tribe in Europe would be predominantly Germanic/Nordic/Slavic as other ethnicities kinfolk is not that easy to come by there. And if there is any kind of pure breed in play, they would lose all of it as well. You . While there definitely are non Indo-Germanic ethnic Garou in the Tribe of the Get i do feel that the majority is still pretty much Indo-Germanic with some Slavic and some Celtic strings as most oft their kinfolk is very likely to be from those regions of the earth where the big majority of the population is Slavic, Germanic or Celtic. </div> </div> </div>Very likely. People traveled an awful lot more in those days than a lot of modern people like to think.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your last sentence is not very straight forward. How much % would you think are non Germanic/Nordic/Slavic Get of Fenris? 7,5-10% in the in total? Maybe between 1/6 and 1/5 in the US? Sounds reasonably to me. </div> </div> </div>First off, the racist camp wouldn't be letting in Slavic Get. Secondly, it doesn't take that many introduced lines to spread further over time. Thirdly, you're assuming that the Get didn't leave trails on the way to getting to Europe, or have breakaways that visited their relatives from time to time. It's not like they were isolationists early on; that didn't come until much, much later, when everyone started getting hemmed in by massive increases in human numbers during the early advent of industry..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do have to say that this reminds me a bit of the controversy that the video game &quot;The Witcher&quot; had, when people felt that there weren't enough PoC.<br /> <br /> What they could conquer some PoC kinfolk and have children with it that should be very clear and while a ton of Kinfolk there are 100% some lines that derived from the sacking of Rome who are Italians and the ones that got conquered from the </div> </div> </div>&quot;Completely white Europe!&quot; is a myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Elitism is not a new concept, they would go with the kinfolk that a.) is available and b.) is strong enough. </div> </div> </div>So why would only the pale ones be strong enough?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think so, as many racists are often still functional members of their societies. </div> </div> </div>Their human societies. Upon being told that their beliefs were all lies, how well do you think they'd react? Especially if saddled with Rage? That may be more likely to be an instance where the Get put a cub down for not being able to hack it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are definitely too brutal for any sensibilities, which would make any individual werewolf that is not of their kin not very likely to join them, wouldn't it? In fact i would think they are one of the tribes that lose the most cubs to other tribes. </div> </div> </div>And one of the few survivors from a bunch of cubs to hold that doctrine would probably end up extremely shocked, possibly to the point of leaving the tribe for somewhere else. Perhaps there wasn't even a rite of passage; they just saw one of their compatriots freak out, get killed, and then decided they'd have better odds in a different place.<br /> <br /> The Garou definitely have a host of foibles and have fucked up the world, but being rampant racists favoring white humans probably shouldn't be one of them, since they're already monsters and pushing it too hard will make the game strangle itself. Lots of spirits would probably avoid you or swat you aside the head for being so concerned about your human identity and trying to make it overwhelm your place as Garou. Also, no coincidentally, most of the ones that would promote it or have no problem? Not the kind of spirits that you would want to be around. Leave the volkisch racism for regional Gangrel who revere the All-High, and their dupes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:26:18-07:00","id":903640,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, if this was a thread about the Get of Fenris, I'd be all over this. But I'm hoping others might want to post about Unicorn or the Children of Gaia, and this is hijacking the thread. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:50:39-07:00","id":903687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Corax didn't get as much revised fluff. They'd probably go into detail about a slightly different setup otherwise, since otherwise the Fenrir would have had a very different reaction to them (see also the things that look like ravens in the story of Uli Brightjaws)</div> </div> </div> </div>That story was a very nice one. I really liked it. The Corax are a great breed, very much usable and versatile. Having more info about them would indeed be great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It had other things to get to, presumably. It can't just talk about this with all of its wordcount.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frigg and Thor are the other two major gods in the Norse/Germanic mythology and as i said i felt it would be nice to see more written about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tyr got his hand bitten off. Tyr isn't of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very certain that he is a Get of Fenris. It is also stated that way on the Get of Fenris wiki page. Or maybe i am misunderstanding things here, please clarify what you mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tribe presumably changed after the experience of fighting the Aesir. Also, they might not have had high numbers at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, but we do not know how much and what changed. But over all i agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Odin,_The_All-High\" target=\"_blank\">a bit worse than that</a> for the Aesir.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Odin, not for everyone else. That said, i was unaware that Odin was a Gangrel and i thank you for providing info.<br /> On the other hand, Loki is a totem spirit for the Nuwisha in W20 CB which is where my guess came from.<br /> <br /> Including that info i would still like the Aesir being Spirits. It would also explain the relationship the Get have with Spirits as a whole and could do some foreshadowing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among might makes right tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but seeing as you did not address the rest of the comment you agree with the rest of the assumption?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very likely. People traveled an awful lot more in those days than a lot of modern people like to think..</div> </div> </div> </div>Who are those &quot;people&quot; anyway. You are using that as a catch all which is getting really tiresome.<br /> <br /> Listen i am not saying that Europe was 100% white. I am saying it is not likely that there was much Kinfolk outside of their home countries that was free to take as other Tribes do not really share them without a fight. I am saying that any kinfolk that would try to travel there from other ethnicities would be scooped up by the Get of Fenris immediately, but those numbers are not thousands per year if you catch my drift.<br /> <br /> As i stated above, i am not saying it does not happen. If you would like to use it hypothetically for a character i would expect it being a strong point in the background story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, the racist camp wouldn't be letting in Slavic Get. Secondly, it doesn't take that many introduced lines to spread further over time. Thirdly, you're assuming that the Get didn't leave trails on the way to getting to Europe, or have breakaways that visited their relatives from time to time. It's not like they were isolationists early on; that didn't come until much, much later, when everyone started getting hemmed in by massive increases in human numbers during the early advent of industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I was pretty sure we were talking about all the Get of Fenris in the world not a specific camp. Was this a misunderstanding on my part.<br /> 2. That depends how you look at it. You are not Chinese because you have - let's say - 1/16 Chinese ancestry, at least that is how it is seen in most of Europe (and to my knowledge).<br /> 3. I did think about them quite a bit. I just thought that other tribes would have scooped them up in the meantime.<br /> 4. That is a good point in my eyes, the increase in human population might have a even stronger implication, i will try to find some estimations on population increase in the varied phases of the earth and we could go from there.<br /> <br /> Would you please give a rough estimation how many Get of Fenris are not part of the stereotypical make up of said tribe? It would show me where you are coming from and is likely to be very effective to understand each others point in this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Completely white Europe!&quot; is a myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see that is a placative statement i have to agree with, but adds nothing to the discussion from my point of view. While there are certainly non &quot;white&quot; ethnicities in Europe in the middle ages there is no need to go full &quot;medievalpoc&quot; on it. This whole line of thinking is ultimately eurocentric. It is less useful to everyone involved trying to find PoCs in a Slavic epos, instead it is way more useful and effective to celebrate the ones that are filled with PoC because they are from regions where you have a majority population of PoC.<br /> <br /> This is kind of off topic though...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why would only the pale ones be strong enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't and i did not want to insinuate that they would not. Was it deliberate of you not to respond to the first part, which is the crux here. It would be pretty bad discussion style in my eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their human societies. Upon being told that their beliefs were all lies, how well do you think they'd react? Especially if saddled with Rage? That may be more likely to be an instance where the Get put a cub down for not being able to hack it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't bad points, but do not convince me. I do think that a racist werewolf might still be able to cut it as a Get of Fenris and the reason are both low rage Werewolves and the different septs in different countries. There might be more sexist or more conservative septs and there might be ones that are less problems in that regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one of the few survivors from a bunch of cubs to hold that doctrine would probably end up extremely shocked, possibly to the point of leaving the tribe for somewhere else. Perhaps there wasn't even a rite of passage; they just saw one of their compatriots freak out, get killed, and then decided they'd have better odds in a different place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things that can happen, but if they should happen is a different question. I mean even the toughest Gets would ask the Garou who massacred cubs without reason, if it wouldn't been better if they were just send to the Bone Gnawer or other tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903611#post903611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Garou definitely have a host of foibles and have fucked up the world, but being rampant racists favoring white humans probably shouldn't be one of them, since they're already monsters and pushing it too hard will make the game strangle itself. Lots of spirits would probably avoid you or swat you aside the head for being so concerned about your human identity and trying to make it overwhelm your place as Garou. Also, no coincidentally, most of the ones that would promote it or have no problem? Not the kind of spirits that you would want to be around. Leave the volkisch racism for regional Gangrel who revere the All-High, and their dupes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of disagree. Get of Fenris Theurges already do hunt down spirits and while i agree that those spirits that like above mentioned ideals can be problematic, but not all of them are banes and therefore it is essential to not let them go that way. That would be something the Get would be really good at.<br /> <br /> The Garou are speciesists and triablists by definition. They committed, helped and/or are responsible for some of the biggest (if not the biggest) Genocides in the history of mankind, but Racists? &quot;Na man let that to go the Gangrel&quot;<br /> <br /> The Garou are not good people and as long as the Get is strong in the eyes of his sept and is able to finish the rite of passage he is in. Racist or not. Black or not. Woman or not.<br /> <br /> I don't say they should be big and i don't say that i would like to play them. That said having them around is in my eyes a byproduct of the ultimate thing a Get should be. Strong. And by sheer rule of probability there will be strong racists who would end up as Get of Fenris.<br /> <br /> For them making a complete camp might be too much, i can meet you half way there, but that they exist and if there is no open Camp there could be a secret one. However the best thing that came out of this discussion from my PoV is that i know understand myself better and know why i feel they lose flavor without them: They are a bunch of fucking crazy warriors who are genocidal maniacs who are described as racist and sexist. Them being suddenly cautious of racism is not really what they are about. If they want to account for the past there are crazier things they did.<br /> <br /> It reminds me a bit of the Soprano plot, where they thought that Jimmy Altieri was a rat and murdered him. After some time they found out that the rat was &quot;Big Pussy&quot; Bonpensiero, but did they question themselves if killing Jimmy was right? No way!<br /> <br /> edit: Sorry @ Black fox my bad. I will stop posting about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:57:24-07:00","id":903791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=902384#post902384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are some points about unicorns in real legend and folklore.<br /> <br /> The essentials of Unicorn as a totem are thus:<ul><li>A paragon and protector of purity.</li> <li>A creature that is untamed and ferocious.</li> <li>A healer as well as a warrior.</li> <li>A magnificent beast who is a natural leader of the wilderness.</li> </ul>\u201cPeace\u201d by itself is not one of its properties, although we can see the reasons why promoting peace became a goal. Originally it was in service of its original totemic goals, but later became a goal in itself \u2013 probably as a result of a particularly successful Camp in pushing its political goals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely love your ideas on Unicorn and the CoG. They speak to pretty much all the problems I have about the tribe, as well as why they are my favorite. I especially like how you are characterizing Unicorn here. Unicorn <i>does</i> want to protect purity, and this includes the &quot;innocent&quot; in a sense. Like you mention, Black Unicorn is a example of how that guardianship can be totally different than the stereotypical captain planet garou. Among my other CoG loving friends, we really identify with Black Unicorn. I want to play a CoG who gets right up in the face of the horrible wyrm shit terrorizing and corrupting people and tear it to shreds. Yes, that means walking the line of your rage... that's the point. That is the test and duty of garou. To deny your rage is to deny part of what and who you are, and what your purpose is. It's to throw away the sword placed in your hands by Luna herself.<br /> <br /> My partner said to me the other day that he thinks the coolest CoG concept is a lupus philadox. After some discussion, I quickly agreed. As a lupus CoG (at least one born and raised in the wild) you have a perspective better suited to understand that there is a difference between balance, and even justice, and peace. Balance, as seen in nature, is not pacifism. Everything must do what it has to do to survive. All of Gaia's creations have their place in the cycle, and that place is NOT necessarily one of peace. The very concept of predators proves that conflict is <i>inherent</i> to nature. There are far too many children of gaia who are aiming for complete peace, and that is not only unfeasible, it isn't natural and never has been. Gaia has her dark sides, much like the dark aspects of the goddess figure in both ancient and neopagan lore. A lupus philadox is in an interesting place to emphasize this point.<br /> <br /> Peace, total peace, leads to stagnation. Total peace is antithetical to life, which <i>must</i> include the wyld, and therefore conflict and challenge. Striving toward that ideal fanatically leads children of Unicorn down very bad paths - see the Bringers of Eternal Peace camp for one example. In our opinion, it could just as easily (and more insidiously) lead children of gaia into the grasp of the weaver.<br /> <br /> One thing I still disagree with many people over is sex between garou and the metis issue. I know, I know. <s> I'm going to take that to a new thread though, because I can see that totally derailing this one as well. </s><br /> EDIT: I have a 1700 word post about the topic, but I'm not going to post it. It's not worth opening that can...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3533-sonofgaia","user":"SonOfGaia","date":". 05-30-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3533-sonofgaia","name":"SonOfGaia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T18:40:26-07:00","id":903889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=902384#post902384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Children of Gaia opposed the Impergium not out of a sense of non-violence... ...This was later twisted \u2013 likely quite lately, perhaps as a result of prolonged exposure to Christianity in Europe during the Dark Ages \u2013 as a general desire for non-violence, peace, or compassion. Means became ends over the course of centuries. This process would be accelerated later as Humanism, the Enlightenment, and international pacifism took hold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so one of the overriding issues that the CoGs have is that they tend to hold (as a matter of tribal ideology) that the War of the Apocalypse cannot be won without first winning the hearts and minds of Humanity at large. If Humanism is no longer (in your interpretation) a core tenet of CoG philosophy, is the battle for the hearts and minds still a priority for the tribe -- and if so, how do they balance that with this more predatory philosophy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T21:06:37-07:00","id":903934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903889#post903889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so one of the overriding issues that the CoGs have is that they tend to hold (as a matter of tribal ideology) that the War of the Apocalypse cannot be won without first winning the hearts and minds of Humanity at large. If Humanism is no longer (in your interpretation) a core tenet of CoG philosophy, is the battle for the hearts and minds still a priority for the tribe -- and if so, how do they balance that with this more predatory philosophy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have not given this any thought before, but I'm fairly agnostic about it. That attitude or idea is not intrinsic to the Unicorn totem, but neither is it antithetical to it. I think it is just one of many ways where the Children of Gaia adopted a means, and that means ends up becoming an end.<br /> <br /> If we see them still as being very concerned about the Defiler Wyrm, as it is a threat to purity and innocence, then combating its influence among humanity easily leads to the idea that the Children need to help/reform humanity to free themselves from it. And Unicorn is about healing as the legends of the healing power of the unicorn horn tells us. So a &quot;this is how we heal humanity from the Defiler Wyrm's corruption&quot; is still broadly appropriate.<br /> <br /> My reason for originally looking at the totem and tribe wasn't to completely invalidate the tribe as is. It was to bring in aspects of the unicorn legend that weren't being used for some reason. And I thought doing so would solve some of the problems many people (including myself) have with the tribe's development.<br /> <br /> So I don't have a problem with that approach by some of the Children, or even many of the Children. But I don't think that was what the tribe was about 5000 or 8000 or 10,000 years ago. Nor do I think that every single member of the tribe today has to believe that as a matter of &quot;tribal politics&quot; or &quot;tribal goals&quot;. I think there are other interpretations or iterations of the tribe that is possible, especially for individual PCs and NPCs. I want to open up the tribe to some other influences.<br /> <br /> This was a good question. Based on the number of likes these posts are getting, I feel like a struck a nerve. So I encourage other people to joint he debate and give their ideas well on this and any other part of the thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T21:23:11-07:00","id":903941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfGaia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903791#post903791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Balance, as seen in nature, is not pacifism. Everything must do what it has to do to survive. All of Gaia's creations have their place in the cycle, and that place is NOT necessarily one of peace. The very concept of predators proves that conflict is <i>inherent</i> to nature. There are far too many children of gaia who are aiming for complete peace, and that is not only unfeasible, it isn't natural and never has been. Gaia has her dark sides, much like the dark aspects of the goddess figure in both ancient and neopagan lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely with this. William Blake summed up it perfectly in The Tyger when he wrote talking of the &quot;fearful symmetry&quot; of the tiger and asking, &quot;Did he who made the lamb make thee?&quot; Real world nature is dangerous, as anyone who has been in a survival situation knows. Mother Nature is not the sanitized depiction in Sea World or the San Diego Zoo. But this facet seems to be curiously absent from too many depictions of the Children of the Gaia with their &quot;My Little Pony&quot; version of Unicorn. I think the Children of Gaia must be comfortable with that aspect of nature, because it is of Gaia.<br /> <br /> I was using Unicorn in my chronicle as a totem of an NPC pack (not even the Children of Gaia), and the PCs were interacting with that pack and totem for the first time. When one PC went into the umbra and met that pack totem, after a brief description I said, &quot;This is <i>not</i> a tamed animal&quot;, the PCs went &quot;whoah.&quot; They GOT IT. As the PCs realized this was not My Little Pony, but a wild animal - like a mustang they were trying to approach safely. It totally changed their perception of what Unicorn was as a totem. They were somewhat in awe and wary. They knew unicorn was benevolent, but dangerous as well. And I liked that.<br /> <br /> To me, that is the real unicorn. The kind of unicorn that would skewer hunters and their dogs when they trespassed into the ancient forest that was unicorn's domain. Yet it is the same kind of unicorn that could be tamed by a virgin maiden. Unicorn protects sacred places and children and the innocent because they are its domain, and it <i>protects</i> what is in its domain. And it is a fierce protector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T11:56:20-07:00","id":904332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=903934#post903934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... But I don't think that was what the tribe was about 5000 or 8000 or 10,000 years ago...</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the fact that I'm sort of happy with the tribe as depicted, I would actually agree with that... but...<br /> <br /> The tribe from its very creation was about peace on at least some level. Maybe not the modern &quot;hippy&quot; concept, but at least by the standards of the day. According to the Children's mythic history, the tribe came into being during a time of internecine warfare among the Garou. During one such battle, five innocent pups were slain. Gaia returned them to life and charged them with bringing peace to the Garou. Now, does that mean turning an entire race of Rage-filled spirit warriors to adopt total pacifism? Mmmmm... probably not. But rather, turn the Garou (and their inherently violent and destructive urges) toward their true enemies -- as in the ones that they were originally created to fight, not mindlessly slaughtering each other. In that sense, the Children (and Unicorn) would be perfectly fine as Rage-filled spirit warriors themselves.<br /> <br /> All well and dandy. Except...<br /> <br /> The Impergium and the War of Rage. When the Garou slaughtered the Gurahl (to the point that most Garou in the modern day assume that they were completely exterminated just like the Apis, Grondr, and Camazotz), they (the Garou) in effect assumed the responsibilities of the shapeshifters they wiped out (or merely decimated). The Gurahl were Gaia's healers and nurturers (particularly of humanity). The CoGs explicitly took those roles upon themselves (basically since who else among the Garou Nation was going to? The Fenrir?). On the other hand, with the severe psychological trauma that the Garou collectively inflicted upon Humanity over the course of three thousand years (in some ways to the point of psychosis), the obvious need to heal that damage, coupled to the fact that the Gurahl (at least apparently) weren't around to do it, meant that the Children (and their totem) needed to show a far more softer side than they had up to that point. If they continued to be their usual old selves, they would wind up sowing more harm than good, given that now doing no more than simply having a modest degree of Rage would at times send humans into screaming fits. Although it's not specifically stated this way, I've always looked upon Black Unicorn as Unicorn splitting that more predatory part of himself off into a separate, distinct element so that he could continue to guide his tribe in it's &quot;new&quot; role.<br /> <br /> That's my interpretation, at least.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:29:28-07:00","id":904650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=904332#post904332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tribe from its very creation was about peace on at least some level.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly canon, and if you have no problems with its standard portrayal, my post probably has little interest for you. Unless there is something you can selectively pick and choose from it.<br /> <br /> My intention is not to create an ALL NEW, ALL DIFFERENT tribe. Ideally, people will still be able to use anything in canon they'd like, but avoid the sometimes tortured efforts to make it into something playable or at least avoid some of the groan inducing moments the tribebooks seem to produce. It seems to be one of the tribes that many players have the most trouble with.<br /> <br /> I don't think Unicorn, as a totem, is about peace. However, as a concept peace is something that often mixes with the things the totem should care about - healing, protection of the innocent, the unspoiled wilderness, etc. As I've said before, I think the tribe's members focus on &quot;peace&quot; is a means that ended up becoming confused for an end for itself.<br /> <br /> The mythic tribal origin of the story isn't necessarily against that. Even under my interpretation, Unicorn could say, &quot;Hey, five innocent Garou cubs were slain because these maniacs are killing each other willy nilly. Therefore, I am going to adopt some Garou as my children with the intention of protecting these innocent cubs.&quot; As part of that remit, those first Coggies could make peace within the tribes important.<br /> <br /> As well as anything else, &quot;making peace&quot; can very well be an important component of Unicorn's desire to heal various people or defend sacred spaces.<br /> <br /> I don't think it invalidates many of the canonical depictions. I think they can work in my interpretation. It's just that I think my ideas opens up the tribe a bit, and its why I posted them. Looking at it differently I think addresses many of the concerns others have about the tribe, even if they are not your own concerns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn?p=904332#post904332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my interpretation, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it is a valid one, and it is certainly the canonical one supported by the game line. I don't think you are wrong for liking that. Everyone's taste is different. For me at least though, changing the totem's &quot;core&quot; role from peace to protecting of the pure/innocent/sacred leads to more positive developments for an ST and PC perspective, and it is certainly better aligned with actual myths and legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T15:33:34-07:00","id":906754,"title":"","content":"Black Fox, I really enjoyed reading what you've put thought to here. Really like it and I hope to see more CoG reflected in this than stoner hippies. Not that there's anything wrong with that, I've just seen it a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}